          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پیک",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پیک (peyk) — \"a courier, a delivery rider\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پیک (peyk) غذا را جلوی در آورد. Peyk ghazâ râ jolow-ye dar âvard. The delivery rider brought the food to the door."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Peyk-e motori — a motorbike courier."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "peyk is inherited: EtymDB traces it to Middle Persian payg, which is usually glossed 'a messenger, a runner'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
